    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21929" root="شدخ" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَادِخٌ</span></b>  A child that is <i>soft,</i> or <i>tender;</i> (K;) as
also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَدَخٌ</span></b> : (IAar, L:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُلَامٌ شَادِخٌ</span> signifies
<i>a youth:</i> (A:) accord. to IAar, a boy is called
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَفْرٌ</span>; then, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَافِعٌ</span>; then, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَدَخٌ</span></b> ; then, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُطَبِّخٌ</span>;
and then, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَوْكَبٌ</span>. (TA. [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُطَبِّخٌ</span>.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
Also A thing, or an affair, <i>deviating from the
right course, aim,</i> or <i>scope,</i> (K, TA,) or <i>from its</i>
[<i>proper</i>] <i>way.</i> (AO, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also the next
paragraph.

